IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc22-at-large`

-- ccc22-tests-at-large.l4 -- tests for ccc22-at-large.l4 (sections 597 to 600). Expected values are written from the text, beside the assertion. Arguments are in the order of each function's GIVEN lines.

§ `Section 597`

-- (1): args: an indictment preferred against a person at large, the person does not appear or remain in attendance, the court is the court before which the accused should have appeared.
#ASSERT `s 597(1) the court may issue a warrant in Form 7 for the arrest of the accused` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 597(1) the court may issue a warrant in Form 7 for the arrest of the accused` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the person is not at large: "Where" fails (ruling (b))
#ASSERT `s 597(1) the court may issue a warrant in Form 7 for the arrest of the accused` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the person appears and remains
#ASSERT `s 597(1) the court may issue a warrant in Form 7 for the arrest of the accused` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another court
#ASSERT `s 597(2) the warrant may be executed anywhere in Canada` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 597(2) the warrant may be executed anywhere in Canada` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): args: arrested under a warrant issued under (1), the person is a judge of the court that issued it.
#ASSERT `s 597(3) a judge of the court that issued the warrant may make a release order referred to in section 515` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 597(3) a judge of the court that issued the warrant may make a release order referred to in section 515` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 597(3) a judge of the court that issued the warrant may make a release order referred to in section 515` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a judge of another court
#ASSERT `s 597(4) the judge may specify the period before which the warrant shall not be executed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 597(4) the judge may specify the period before which the warrant shall not be executed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): args: a warrant has been issued under (1), the accused appears voluntarily.
#ASSERT `s 597(5) the warrant is deemed to be executed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 597(5) the warrant is deemed to be executed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 597(5) the warrant is deemed to be executed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 598`

-- (1): args: 597(1) applies, elected or deemed elected to be tried by judge and jury, had re-elected, excuse established, the Attorney General requires a jury.
#ASSERT `s 598(1) the subsection bars trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 598(1) the subsection bars trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) a legitimate excuse
#ASSERT `s 598(1) the subsection bars trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) the Attorney General requires a jury
#ASSERT `s 598(1) the subsection bars trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- had re-elected to be tried without a jury: the "where" of the bar fails
#ASSERT `s 598(1) the subsection bars trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 597(1) does not apply
#ASSERT `s 598(1) the subsection bars trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- never elected a jury trial
#ASSERT `s 598(2) the accused is deemed to have elected to be tried without a jury by a judge, and section 561 or 561.1 does not apply` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 598(2) the accused is deemed to have elected to be tried without a jury by a judge, and section 561 or 561.1 does not apply` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 598(2) the accused is deemed to have elected to be tried without a jury by a judge, and section 561 or 561.1 does not apply` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 599`

-- (1): args: the application is by the prosecutor or the accused, the other division is in the same province, expedient to the ends of justice, a competent authority has directed that no jury be summoned.
#ASSERT `s 599(1) the court or judge may order the trial to be held in another territorial division in the same province` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 599(1) the court or judge may order the trial to be held in another territorial division in the same province` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 599(1) the court or judge may order the trial to be held in another territorial division in the same province` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither (a) nor (b)
#ASSERT `s 599(1) the court or judge may order the trial to be held in another territorial division in the same province` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not on an application of the prosecutor or the accused
#ASSERT `s 599(1) the court or judge may order the trial to be held in another territorial division in the same province` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in the same province
#ASSERT `s 599(2) what the text shows` EQUALS "[Repealed, R.S., 1985, c. 1 (4th Supp.), s. 16]"
#ASSERT `s 599(3) the court or judge may prescribe conditions respecting the payment of additional expenses caused to the accused` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 599(3) the court or judge may prescribe conditions respecting the payment of additional expenses caused to the accused` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an order on the accused's application
-- (4): args: an order is made under (1), the officer has custody.
#ASSERT `s 599(4) the officer must transmit the indictment, writings and exhibits forthwith to the clerk of the court before which the trial is ordered to be held` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 599(4) the officer must transmit the indictment, writings and exhibits forthwith to the clerk of the court before which the trial is ordered to be held` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 599(4) the officer must transmit the indictment, writings and exhibits forthwith to the clerk of the court before which the trial is ordered to be held` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 599(4) all proceedings in the case are held, or if previously commenced are continued, in the court to which the trial is moved` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 599(4) all proceedings in the case are held, or if previously commenced are continued, in the court to which the trial is moved` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 599(5) the person who obtains the order must serve a true copy on the person in whose custody the writings and exhibits are, who must then transmit them to the clerk` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 599(5) the person who obtains the order must serve a true copy on the person in whose custody the writings and exhibits are, who must then transmit them to the clerk` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 600`

-- args: an order is made under section 599, the person is a sheriff, a keeper of a prison or a peace officer, the act is the removal, disposal or reception in accordance with the order.
#ASSERT `s 600 the order is sufficient warrant, justification and authority for the act` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 600 the order is sufficient warrant, justification and authority for the act` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 600 the order is sufficient warrant, justification and authority for the act` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 600 the order is sufficient warrant, justification and authority for the act` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an act outside the terms of the order
#ASSERT `s 600 the sheriff may appoint and authorize a peace officer to convey the accused to a prison` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 600 the sheriff may appoint and authorize a peace officer to convey the accused to a prison` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 600 the sheriff may appoint and authorize a peace officer to convey the accused to a prison` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 600 the sheriff may appoint and authorize a peace officer to convey the accused to a prison` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a prison outside the division where the trial is ordered
